<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH Q1 GDP CONFIRMED AT 2.1 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>DUTCH Q1 GDP CONFIRMED AT 2.1 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch first</p>
<p>quarter gross domestic product (GDP) rose 2.1 percent</p>
<p>year-on-year, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said,</p>
<p>confirming provisional figures released in May.</p>
<p>DUTCH GDP</p>
<p>		    Q1 97	 Q4 96	 Q3 96	 Q2 96</p>
<p> year-on-year   +2.1 (+2.1) +3.0 (+3.0) +3.1 (+3.1) +3.2 (+3.2)</p>
<p>vs previous qtr</p>
<p> (seas. adj.)   -0.5 (-0.6) +0.5 (+0.5) +0.7 (+0.7) +1.3 (+1.5)</p>
<p>DUTCH GDP IN DETAIL</p>
<p> (real pct change yr/yr)	Q1 97  Q4 96  Q3 96  Q2 96</p>
<p> private consumption	    2.6    2.9    2.6    2.7</p>
<p> government consumption	 1.3    0.9    0.6    0.5</p>
<p> business investment	   11.6   12.1    8.9    3.7</p>
<p> government investment	  8.9    4.6    5.9    6.9</p>
<p> exports goods and services   3.3    2.0    1.2    1.0</p>
<p> imports goods and services   3.7    2.1    1.7    1.4</p>
<p>DUTCH GDP - INVESTMENT IN DETAIL</p>
<p> (real pct change yr/yr)	 Q1 97  Q4 96  Q3 96  Q2 96</p>
<p> total gross fixed investment 11.2   11.0    8.5    4.1</p>
<p> housing			    22.4    9.1    2.4    2.9</p>
<p> other buildings		  17.3    7.2    5.1   13.0</p>
<p> roads, waterways etc.	   8.0    4.6    5.8    8.4</p>
<p> transport equipment	     5.4   10.1    0.9  -13.1</p>
<p> machinery			   6.7   13.1   18.5    3.1</p>
<p>NOTE - CBS said the growth figure for GDP during the first</p>
<p>quarter was distorted by the fact that there were fewer working</p>
<p>days, adding the underlying growth was 3.0 to 4.0 percent. </p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 570 8500</p>
</text>
